---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About" description="About AI-Dialogos, the AI Essentials for Leaders book series, and series co-editors Alfred Essa and Teresa Martín-Retortillo.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-12 rounded-3xl bg-white/90 p-8 shadow-card sm:p-10">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-[#1b5ed8]">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#113e8c]">AI-Dialogos</h1>
      <div class="h-px w-full bg-[#1b5ed8]/60"></div>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
      <p>
        <strong>AI-Dialogos</strong> is the companion platform for the <em>AI Essentials for Leaders</em> book series, published by <a href="https://www.degruyterbrill.com" class="text-[#1b5ed8] underline decoration-dotted" target="_blank" rel="noopener">De Gruyter Brill</a>. The series offers concise, non-technical primers for navigating the complex world of Artificial Intelligence — written by leading experts for business leaders, practitioners, policymakers, and curious learners.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site brings together curated resources around the series: Substack essays that explore AI topics in depth, a video podcast featuring conversations with leaders and innovators, and information on each volume as it is released.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name <em>Dialogos</em> — from the Greek <em>dialogos</em> (dialogue) — reflects our belief that the most important questions about AI are best explored through open, ongoing conversation across disciplines and perspectives.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="space-y-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">The Series</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
        <p>
          Each volume in <em>AI Essentials for Leaders</em> synthesizes a foundational AI topic through a focused lens — technology fundamentals, business strategy, entrepreneurship, leadership and governance, or ethics and privacy. The goal is to give leaders the conceptual clarity they need to make informed decisions about AI adoption, strategy, and governance.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/series" class="text-[#1b5ed8] underline decoration-dotted">View the full series overview and themes.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="space-y-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Series Co-Editors</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-7 text-[#113453]">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Alfred Essa</h3>
          <p>
            Alfred Essa has led pioneering AI and advanced analytics teams across academia and industry. As Simon Fellow at Carnegie Mellon University, VP of Analytics and R&D at McGraw Hill Education, and CIO at MIT's Sloan School of Management, he has bridged the gap between theoretical innovation and practical implementation.
          </p>
          <p>
            He is the author of <em>Artificial Intelligence: Shaping the Future of Innovation</em> (De Gruyter Brill, 2025) and <em>Practical AI for Business Leaders, Product Managers, and Entrepreneurs</em>. He holds degrees from Haverford College and Yale University.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-7 text-[#113453]">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Teresa Martín-Retortillo</h3>
          <p>
            Teresa Martín-Retortillo is a senior executive with deep global experience in strategy and innovation, spanning executive boards and boards of directors of both private and listed companies. After two decades advising private equity investors and global corporations, she has spent the last decade executing digital business models.
          </p>
          <p>
            Her work at Goldman Sachs, Bain and Company, McGraw Hill Education, and IE University has made her a sought-after thought leader. She is the author of <em>Artificial Intelligence: Rethinking Business Strategy</em> (De Gruyter Brill, 2026). She is a graduate of Harvard Business School.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Get in Touch</h2>
      <div class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
        <p>
          If you have proposals for submission or ideas you would like to discuss, please contact series co-editor Alfred Essa at
          <a href="mailto:aessa@ai-essentials-for-leaders.com" class="ml-1 text-[#1b5ed8] underline decoration-dotted">aessa@ai-essentials-for-leaders.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
